					</td>
					<td id="JoinCell" width="100%" valign="top"><STRONG>Members:<!--EZCODE BOLD END--><BR><BR></STRONG>Velious Faction: Giant. We intend to do conquer and explore all the high end material that's out there, and for velious this is much much easier achieved when allying with Giants, due to ST/NToV. Being allied with giants is just more fun <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/smile.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> . This doesn't mean you're actually *required* to be allied with giants, and have good faction with them - it merely means that you can't have ties to CoV that prevent you from participating in kills.<BR><BR>This means no /q'ing out on faction mobs. There are *very* limited occasions where this can be done - take for example Dozekar quests. Yes, I intend on killing that thing, so what we expect is this; You attend raids, you do not /q out for faction reasons until you have ALL the required quest items to complete the quest. At that point, you are allowed to /q out on faction mobs, and you may do so until you have your item. You may have a given deadline that may be contingent upon targets we kill, but I expect you to be very active in pursuing that faction so you can get back with us on the dark side <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :evil --><IMG alt=:evil src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/devil.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> . Faction really isn't *that* hard to switch around.<BR><BR><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><B>For applicants:</B><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> If you are an applicant to our guild, you are expressing desire to be part of the guild and therefore abide by our loot rules as if you were guilded. This means I expect you not to be /q'ing out unless you have an certain case where you are holding armor for your previous guild, etc. Just talk to me, I'm flexible enough <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/smile.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> . <BR><BR><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><B>Loot policy:</B><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> At this time, the officers and I after much consideration of issues have decided on this - We are adopting a master-loot system for key items and key classes where loot at times will be assigned by officers to specific people/classes, especially in the early months when we need to gear up key classes for harder encounters. The rest of the items will be class-appropriate and quite class-specific random. There are many benefits in an RPP system, but there are many problems also. We don't want to see a sense of in-guild competition, and we don't want to see decent items rotting because no one wants to roll on them. This means I am trusting YOU to police yourselves at times. That means if something drops and you have won recently, I'm going to expect people to be gracious enough to back out on rolls at the appropriate times. Sometimes you won't when something incredible comes along - that is understood. We all know when we've had our share of luck. <BR><BR><!--EZCODE BOLD START--><B>For non-guildies (non-applicants):</B><!--EZCODE BOLD END--> If we specifically ask you to come along and join us on a raid, when otherwise you would be helping your own guild or the like, you will get a roll in loot that has dropped. This means loot that is randomed. Occasionally, when the guild has 66% majority (members only, not applicants) I will consider it an Oryx driven raid, and I *may* choose to default a drop to a key class or person. ST keys follow this rule also, but I will consider an Oryx majority against people from ST capable guilds, i.e. 30 person raid - 16 Oryx, 3 from ST capable guild x, 6 applicants, 5 friends from random guilds. I consider us to have the power to default keys, due to 16/3 = more than enough majority. Additionally, you are also allowed to /q out for faction reasons, though we encourage you to just refaction if at all possible <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/smile.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> .<BR><BR>Some of you have expressed to me thoughts that RPP encourages attendance and committment. I see no reason why I need to encourage attendance from people who want to be there <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/smile.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> . Frankly, you all are here because I think you have stated your level of committment to having fun and enjoying a raiding game. I stated elsewhere that guild health &gt; all, and people need to realize when personal desires are compromising this, but I want people to have a sense of individual accomplishment also.<BR><BR>Regarding Alts/mains/alts who are upcoming mains and loot policy-<BR><BR>Applicants for our guild will be considered if they are 58+. As to how that applies to current member's alts, alts who are upcoming mains will not be considered for loot until they at least that level. Minimum raid level is 55 for alts, you can bring an alt and roll on stuff for your main, but your alt starts getting consideration on loot (and not for rolling against mains) at that level. Unless something is gonna rot, I will bank stuff for guildbank MQ funds unless your alt is 55. This is to consider not only the ability of that character to contribute to raids, but also the average level of present mains contributing (which is very nearly 60 atm) against your upcoming character.<BR><BR>Always remember most of all, we're here to have fun <!--EZCODE EMOTICON START :) --><IMG alt=:) src=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/images/emoticons/smile.gif><!--EZCODE EMOTICON END--> . <br></td>

